fact WorkItem(id: "WI-821", description: some(value: "FIX the call-site requirement-supply defect that WI-817's witness measured: a caller's dictionary is FORWARDED into a callee requirement slot whose element the call-site substitution maps to a DIFFERENT type. MECHANISM (verified in source): build_dep_projection (kb/typing.rs, ~11404) Strategy 1's entries_cover is WILDCARD-TOLERANT — a caller (requires Desc[GT]) covers a callee dep (Desc[FT]) whenever either element is a type param — and the WI-419 sigma-class check (disambiguate_covering_by_sigma) runs ONLY to break ties between 2+ covering entries, never to REJECT a sole one; so a single covering wildcard entry blindly emits var_ref(__req_desc), forwarding the caller's dictionary and SHADOWING Strategy 3, whose SLD construction of the Conditional tree (resolve_inner + emit_tree_as_projection) handles the changed type correctly when reached. MEASURED CONSEQUENCES, pinned in rustland/anthill-core/tests/include/wi817_polyrec_requirement_test.rs: (1) sort_level_recursion_silently_wrong_control_and_lambda_identical — polymorphic recursion (g re-enters f at Wrap[GT]) returns 1 at EVERY depth (correct: 1, 12, 122); the Leaf dictionary rides the whole recursion, the conditional WrapDesc instance is never consulted, and the Leaf impl runs on wrapped values — outcome (d), silent wrong answers on a clean load; (2) lambda_relay_chain_closure_correct_but_hop_dicts_forwarded — with ALL-CONCRETE bindings and no recursion, a relay chain measures 111 instead of 551: the closure half is CORRECT (the creation dictionary held across two foreign frames) while BOTH hops' own dictionaries arrive wrongly forwarded — so the defect is NOT confined to changed-type recursion; it hits ANY same-spec cross-instantiation call whenever the caller holds a covering wildcard entry. THE FIX (Rule A, WI-817 Deliverable 2): make sigma-class agreement a GATE on forwarding, in Strategy 1 AND Strategy 2's sub-chain matching (same predicate): a covering entry may be forwarded only when the dep's element sigma-resolves to the SAME unification class as the entry's element; a DISAGREEING sole entry is NO COVER and falls through to Strategy 3's construction — for the recursion that emits construct_requirement(WrapDesc, [var_ref(__req_desc)]), the Conditional-with-FromScope-leaf tree. The sigma machinery already computes exactly this agreement for the 2+ case — the change is consulting it for ONE covering entry and treating disagreement as no-cover rather than keeping first-match. WATCH: same-class forwarding must STAY — it is the dominant correct case (wi418 abstract forwarding, wi419 disambiguation, every delegating stdlib body) and must keep forwarding BY NAME, not re-constructing; and the sigma-less diagnostic path (req_insertion passes disambig = None) must keep today's behaviour — gate only when a call-site substitution is in hand, and say why at the site. ACCEPTANCE: the two (d) pins in wi817_polyrec_requirement_test.rs FLIP and are updated to assert their documented CORRECT values (recursion: 1/12/122 per depth, for the control AND the lambda witness; relay chain: 551); sort_level_single_conditional_level_is_correct stays green (12); wi418/wi419/wi613 forwarding suites stay green (no regression of same-class forwarding); full workspace green via rustland/scripts/test.sh. OUT OF SCOPE, deliberately (already recorded as siblings in WI-817 feedback, to be filed separately): the op-scoped channel parity (outcome-c pins — no call-site supply channel for op-scoped chains; value-directed dispatch pushes impl frames dict-less) and the op-param requires coverage gap (outcome-b pins, spec par. 5.4); those pins stay pinning under this ticket and flip only under their own tickets. RELATION: WI-817 is REOPENED and depends on THIS ticket — its remaining deliverable is the REMEASURE of the committed witness after this lands, which finally answers the original operation-vs-lambda prediction and supplies WI-816 its evidence; WI-816 stays behind WI-817."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-23T11:57:29Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-821", author: "user", content: "SHARPEST ACCEPTANCE TARGET, added after a user-directed probe (pinned as different_sets_overlapping_dep_forwarded_disjoint_dep_constructed in the WI-817 suite): a hand-off between operations with DIFFERENT requirement sets — caller (Desc[AT]) to callee (Desc[BT], Tagd[BT]) at concrete BT := Pebble — measures 31001 today vs 35001 correct: in ONE call the overlapping dep is wildcard-forwarded WRONG while the disjoint dep is Strategy-3-constructed RIGHT. This is live in-fixture proof that the fall-through this ticket gates to ALREADY WORKS for the very call whose sibling dep is being mis-forwarded; the sigma-gate only has to stop the overlap-forward. ACCEPTANCE addition: this pin flips to 35001.", at: "2026-07-23T10:07:49Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-821", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED. The ticket's stated fix (gate Strategies 1/2) was NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT — the first gate attempt changed NOTHING observable (all three defect pins kept measuring 31001/111/1). The wildcard tolerance has FOUR sites, each re-creating the forward when the previous is gated: (1) Strategy 1 entries_cover — gated; (2) Strategy 2 sub-chains — gated on the sub-entry COMPOSED into caller scope (build_child_subst_map + substitute_in_spec; raw slot-space entries would sigma-disagree on CORRECT nested forwards); (3) resolve_inner's scope loop (requires_entry_covers_goal) — Strategy 3's FromScope short-circuits before provider candidates and emitted the IDENTICAL var_ref(__req_desc); sigma now rides ResolutionScope and gates it; (4) match_candidate_against_goal's WI-507 leniency left a Var::Rigid per-call element UNBOUND, so the conditional instance's sub-goal kept the raw impl param and died Cyclic — the rigid is now RECORDED (first-writer-wins; a stored rigid yields to an incoming concrete for order symmetry). The sigma-precise predicates are FOLDED into entries_cover/requires_entry_covers_goal as an Option<&SigmaCtx> mode (sigma-precise implies coarse; one walk decides) so the coarse and gating covers cannot drift. ACCEPTANCE DEVIATION, resolved in-ticket: the lambda WITNESS could not flip by supply-gating alone — inside the lambda the binder types from the declared hint with apply_fn's X unpinned (args typed before the per-call subst exists), so the inner f-call's dict was built against a wildcard. Fixed by generalizing WI-793 staging: a non-HOF arg pinning a callee type param (op-scoped AND parent-sort params, via elem_var_step) mentioned by a HOF param's type is typed first, and hint_instantiation_subst instantiates the lambda hint from the known sibling types (per-pair scratch-sigma probe so a failed pair's partial bindings cannot corrupt the hint). All three pins flipped and renamed: sort_level_recursion_correct_control_and_lambda_identical (1/12/122 both), lambda_relay_chain_closure_and_hop_dicts_correct (551), different_sets_overlapping_dep_and_disjoint_dep_both_constructed (35001); sort_level_single_conditional stays 12; op-scoped (b)/(c) pins and the value-directed 551 unchanged; wi418/wi419/wi613/wi227/wi224 green; full workspace 3464 passed 0 failed. SIBLING GAP recorded (no pin, no ticket): DeferToRequirement slot attribution (disambiguate_slot_by_sigma) keeps the soft pick_precise fall-back — a sole covering param-vs-DIFFERENT-param entry still attributes a body call and reads a sigma-disagreeing dict at runtime (WI-414 guards only concrete-vs-wildcard). Same silent-wrong class one site over; gating it changes classification outcomes (Deferred -> MissingRequires), so it needs its own measurement-first ticket.", at: "2026-07-23T11:57:30Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-821", author: "user", content: "/code-review (max): 15 findings reported (8 correctness CONFIRMED by live drives — two against a HEAD~1 worktree — 3 correctness PLAUSIBLE, 2 efficiency, 1 simplification, 1 test-coverage); 6 finder candidates REFUTED by driving (arrow-literal staging inertness, Node-carrier forward regression, σ-less-dispatch rigid mis-wiring, cross-namespace raw sort gate — that drive also re-validated the fix across 2- and 3-namespace splits — explicit-type-arg rigid spelling, positional-shorthand empty bindings). MECHANICALLY FIXED in the follow-up commit: the σ/coarse pair verdict folded into ONE binding_pair_covers (kills the drift channel between entries_cover and requires_entry_covers_goal, and gives WI-825 a single fix locus); hint_instantiation_subst probe now clones the ACCUMULATED σ and commits atomically (closes the cross-pair pollution, halves the unify work — Substitution::clone is O(1) imbl); op_tp_pinning_params kind-gates the parent lookup on SymbolKind::Sort and reads the memoized sort_type_params_as_pairs instead of the per-call full-symbol-table type_params_of_sort scan; Strategy 2's σ arm composes lazily and only for same-sort candidates (map at most once per slot, never for leaf-spec empty chains, no allocating compose for sort-mismatched entries); wi817 header pin inventory completed (two_describers) and the covers_goal doc's misattributed fold history corrected; NEW TEST sort_param_applier_witness_matches_control pins the parent-SORT-param staging half at 1/12/122 (was documented-but-unmeasured — it passes, the mechanism works). FILED for the non-trivial families: WI-825 (compound-element σ-blindness — the (d) defect one constructor level deeper, measured 12-vs-122), WI-826 (cover-walk orientation holes — bare bindingless requires bypass measured 1010001-vs-5010001, partial-binding asymmetry, empty-map Strategy-2 no-op), WI-827 (candidate-matching σ integration — Ref-spelled compound Cyclic, two-distinct-rigids half-wrong dict, head-only yield granularity, arm-2.5 symmetry), WI-828 (σ-refusal of unconstrained elements must be a load-time diagnostic — measured regressions Ok(11)→runtime-Internal and Ok(4)→unexplained WI-420). CONSCIOUSLY SKIPPED as minor (recorded here, no ticket): eagerly-formatted never-read NoMatch/Cyclic/Ambiguous diagnostic Strings (lazy formatting = ResolutionResult enum change); the wasted resolve_type_deep_value for VarRef-in-non-arrow slots (safe gate needs a σ-mention walk); narrowing the staging trigger to intersected tp sets (behavior-order change); ResolutionScope named constructors; threading the op symbol on OperationInfoFull instead of beside it.", at: "2026-07-23T13:21:29Z")
